+
+## Private swarm integration work
+
+The original status39/40/41 swarm state and shared controller clock are now decoded and under private integration. The empty-hive gameplay binding and swarm damage/presentation/input remain unfinished; the earlier statement that the status itself is unestablished is historical. The private scene scheduler preserves clock/swarm state across Jungle/Hive handoffs without a second timer.
+
+Original media can be reproduced without external review scripts:
+
+```
+python3 tools/prepare_beehive_frames.py --game GAME_ROOT --out FRESH_FRAMES_DIR
+python3 tools/pack_beehive_swarm.py --source FRESH_FRAMES_DIR --out assets/lol2/generated/beehive_swarm
+python3 tools/prepare_beehive_audio.py --game GAME_ROOT --out assets/lol2/generated/beehive_swarm_audio
+```
+
+Each output directory must be new. The 91 frames (66 fly-in, 15 loiter, 10 swat) preserve original indexed pixels and alpha in seven atlases. Audio uses the original codec99 arithmetic and PCM hashes verified against native execution: 95,988 valid samples total; one undefined final sample of flies1 is omitted. These media checks do not establish playback lifetime/gain or modern viewport placement.
+
+### Private health boundary (2026-10-25)
+
+`beehive_player_damage.gd` stages health without changing live owners. It binds
+current health, current form and actually carried equipped items; native UI mode,
+boost/optional/bypass flags, difficulty and entry/continuation flags are still
+explicit caller inputs. The current catalog's only nonidentity bee equipment
+operation is Burnt Chain's `(6,8,4)` in the armor slot; the catalog regression
+checks that assumption before relying on the modern equipment order.
+
+After native mitigation and virtual84 adjustment, positive lethal damage with
+player byte227 bit128 retains one health. Ordinary lethal damage exposes health0
+to the modern death flow. Original survival UI and later native death effects are
+not reproduced here. The checked continuation requires player mode1AB and flags19A
+both zero; other values refuse instead of silently choosing the ordinary branch.
+2,048 positive-health original commit fixtures cover all byte227 values, five
+original health levels (excluding the zero-health entry), and loss1/2. The separate
+zero-health fixture branch is not a damage request and is not used to resurrect a
+player. Health, status clock, audio and presentation still need a single live
+commit boundary before gameplay swarm activation is enabled.
